# M4.24 final review — local hardened-test failure

Date: 2026-08-28

## Failure

The first post-hardening M4.24-only run completed 34 tests with four errors.
Three execution-flow tests stopped before any mocked start because the local
Python build does not accept `follow_symlinks` on `Path.stat`. One postcheck
fixture returned the pre-hardening constant archive value instead of the
archive value captured in its synthetic `before` snapshot.

## Cause

- Portability error in the newly added file-identity helper. `Path.lstat()` is
  the compatible no-follow operation needed here.
- Test-fixture mismatch after replacing aggregate database evidence with a
  complete stable-boundary snapshot.

## Safety impact

None on a host or service. The run was local, mocked, and stopped before the
mocked start command. No deployment, unit action, provider action or contract
approval occurred. The committed PR head remains unchanged and NO-GO.

## Minimal correction

Use `Path.lstat()` and add the exact archive/unit boundary values to the local
synthetic preflight fixture. Rerun M4.24 tests before any broader regression.

## Rollback

